title: blocked is a string in karr but a bool plus block_reason in kanban-md
updated: 2026-08-10T01:40:24Z
---

karr models `blocked` as a free-text string; kanban-md models it as
`Blocked bool` plus `BlockReason string` (`../kanban-md/internal/task/task.go`).
Affected: `Task.pm:53/106`, `Cmd/Edit.pm:188`, `Cmd/Handoff.pm:122`.

karr -> kanban-md (real binary):

    Warning: skipping malformed file 002-blocked-task.md:
      ... cannot unmarshal !!str `waiting...` into bool
    kanban list -> task missing entirely;  kanban show 2 -> rc=1

kanban-md -> karr (file with `blocked: true` / `block_reason: upstream outage`):

    karr show 1 -> "Blocked:  1"          # reason gone
    git show <ref>:data -> block_reason absent   # destroyed on karr's first write

Side effect inside karr: `--json` reports `blocked` sometimes as a string
(`"waiting on API"`), sometimes as a boolean (`true`) — an unstable field type
for anything parsing it.

Fix: adopt the kanban-md shape (`blocked` boolean + `block_reason`), migrate
existing string values on read, and keep `--block "reason"` as the CLI spelling
that sets both.
Fixed and merged into main (3dac607); full suite green at 93 files / 630 tests.
Reproduced before the fix, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix
code. Note the #68 trigger change: started is now stamped on the first move out
of the FIRST CONFIGURED status, per kanban-md lifecycle.go, not out of the
literal in-progress.
